Make DECCOLM never resize the terminal.

Phi needs this because only the layout sets a pane's size. A program in a
pane must not change it. With DEC mode 40 off, DECCOLM still does nothing,
as upstream. With mode 40 on, DECCOLM sets mode 3 and resets the margins,
erases the display, and homes the cursor, but keeps the size. The removed
resize path was what reset the margins, so the patch resets them the same
way resize does.

xterm behaves the same way when its disallowedWindowOps resource includes
ColumnMode: with mode 40 on, srm_DECCOLM in charproc.c still sets the mode
and clears the screen, but skips the resize.

Upstream: https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty/blob/83edd491e3024ae5e50393d62877b8897da1cccd/src/terminal/Terminal.zig#L3970

--- a/src/terminal/Terminal.zig
+++ b/src/terminal/Terminal.zig
@@ -3979,14 +3979,15 @@
     // Enable it
     self.modes.set(.@"132_column", mode == .@"132_cols");
 
-    // Resize to the requested size
-    try self.resize(alloc, .{
-        .cols = switch (mode) {
-            .@"132_cols" => 132,
-            .@"80_cols" => 80,
-        },
-        .rows = self.rows,
-    });
+    // phi: the pane size belongs to the layout, so DECCOLM never resizes.
+    // Reset the margins as resize does.
+    _ = alloc;
+    self.scrolling_region = .{
+        .top = 0,
+        .bottom = self.rows - 1,
+        .left = 0,
+        .right = self.cols - 1,
+    };
 
     // Erase our display and move our cursor.
     self.eraseDisplay(.complete, false);
